--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/recording.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Recording noodlets
+
+Noodle Applet films a noodlet frame by frame. It does not sample the web
+view in real time, so a recording stays smooth when the window is hidden,
+covered or on another space.
+
+## How it works
+
+1. `record-start` puts the page on a virtual clock (`Animation.js`).
+2. For each frame, Recording advances the clock by 1/fps seconds.
+3. Due timers run in order, then animation frame callbacks run with the
+   frame's timestamp, and CSS animations are moved to the same time.
+4. The page reports that the frame has rendered; FrameCapture takes the
+   snapshot and the movie writer appends it at frame number / fps.
+5. `record-stop` returns the page to real time and finishes the movie.
+
+Nothing on the page moves between steps, so a slow snapshot never shows
+up as a stutter. A slow noodlet takes longer to record, but the movie
+still plays at full speed.
+
+## Limits
+
+- Audio is suspended while filming and is not part of the movie.
+- Video elements and workers keep running in real time.
+- Recordings stop after 60 seconds of virtual time.
+
+## Debugging
+
+`noodle-applet logs NOODLET` shows one line for every frame that the page
+did not render in time, with the virtual time it was waiting for.
